<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>

This assert statement checks that if the collection `c` is not empty, then every element in the newly created `ArrayList` is equal to the corresponding element in the array obtained from `c.toArray()`. This ensures that the `ArrayList` contains the same elements as the collection `c` in the same order.
--------------------
<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => this.size() == c.size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => this.size() == c.size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
